# WordPress PHP Conventions

See `edminboost-compliance.mdc` for the security gate; `edminboost-command-center.mdc` for CC patterns.

## File Header

Every PHP file must start with:

```php
<?php
/**
 * Brief description.
 *
 * @package EdminBoost
 */

if ( ! defined( 'ABSPATH' ) ) {
	exit;
}
```

## Security

- Check capabilities before rendering admin pages: `current_user_can( EDMINBOOST_Settings::CAPABILITY )`.
- Escape output: `esc_html()`, `esc_attr()`, `esc_url()`, `esc_html__()`, `esc_html_e()`.
- Sanitize all settings via `EDMINBOOST_Settings::sanitize()` as `sanitize_callback` in `register_setting()`.
- Settings API: `show_in_rest => false`, `wp_unslash()` on array input in sanitize.
- Use nonces for custom form/AJAX handlers (`wp_nonce_field`, `check_admin_referer`).

## WordPress APIs

- Register hooks in `EDMINBOOST_Plugin::run()` or feature `register_hooks()` — not in the bootstrap file.
- Use Settings API for options (`register_setting`, `add_settings_section`, `add_settings_field`).
- Enqueue assets with `EDMINBOOST_VERSION` as the version string.
- Pass data to JS via `wp_localize_script()` — `edminboostData` on plugin screens; `edminboostCcBar` on the live CC bar drawer script.
- Page slugs: use `EDMINBOOST_Admin::PAGE_SLUG` and `EDMINBOOST_Command_Center::PAGE_*` suffixes.

## Class Wiring

- Bootstrap requires core classes; instantiate only via `edminboost_run_plugin()`.
- `EDMINBOOST_Plugin` constructor: `EDMINBOOST_I18n`, `EDMINBOOST_Features`, `EDMINBOOST_Admin`.
- Command Center: `EDMINBOOST_Command_Center` (static helpers, no hooks).
- Command Center Bar: `EDMINBOOST_Command_Center_Bar::register_hooks()` in `EDMINBOOST_Plugin::run()` — not part of the feature registry.
- New productivity modules: extend `EDMINBOOST_Feature_Base`, register in `EDMINBOOST_Features` (see `edminboost-features.mdc`).
- Settings: `EDMINBOOST_Settings::get()`, `::is_enabled()`, `::is_feature_enabled()`, `::get_feature_settings()`.
- Activation seeds defaults via `EDMINBOOST_Activator`; deactivation is a no-op.

## Settings Option Shape

```php
array(
	'enabled'        => true,
	'command_center' => array(
		'onboarding_completed' => false,
		'persona'              => '',
		'top_bar_items'        => array(),
		'presets'              => array(),
		'default_preset'       => 'system_client',
		'role_assignments'     => array(),
		'role_visibility'      => array(),
		'behavior'             => array(
			'drawer_width'         => 'standard',  // compact | standard | fullscreen
			'animation_speed'      => 'normal',    // fast | normal | slow
			'glassmorphism'        => false,
			'autosave_interval'    => 60,
			'badge_refresh_rate'   => 60,
			'badge_style'          => 'pill',      // dot | pill | accent
			'hide_wp_logo'         => false,
			'hide_update_counters' => false,
			'hide_howdy'           => false,
			'hide_comments'        => false,
		),
	),
	'features'       => array(
		'hide_admin_notices' => false,
		'dashboard_widgets'  => array( /* remove_* keys */ ),
		'admin_menu'         => array( 'hidden_items' => array() ),
		'admin_footer'       => array( 'enabled' => false, 'text' => '' ),
		'disable_emojis'     => false,
		'admin_bar'          => array( /* hide_* keys */ ),
	),
)
```

## Partials

- Dashboard: `edminboost-admin-page.php` — expects `$settings`, `$features`.
- Settings: `edminboost-settings-features.php` — expects `$settings`.
- Command Center pages: expect `$cc_settings`, `$current_page` (set by `render_command_center_page()`).
- Document `@var` annotations at the top of partials.

## Docblocks

Document all public methods with `@param`, `@return`, and `@var` on class properties.
